I built the issue desk in `/tmp/claude-0/runs/r15/desk9-contract-haiku-4/app.contract` (view) and `app.ts` (data module, which wraps `src/api.js`), covering all three pages with optimistic edits that revert on a declined write. `./check` compiles clean and `./test` passes all 30 visible tests (2 of 15 runs used). Unsure points: the tabs are state-driven rather than Exact routes, so the pages have no URLs; writes go through one queue per kind, so a second write of the same kind waits for the first; and the hidden tests may check exact wording or error placement, such as the assign error showing only `declined`.